# emu-cpu: the CPU server.  No Cocoa, no graphics, no window.
#
# There are two emu builds on this platform and the difference is not
# cosmetic:
#
#	emu-cocoa  links Cocoa, creates an NSApplication, draws in a
#	           window.  Installed as `emu' as well, and is what you
#	           want at a terminal.
#	emu-cpu    links no Cocoa at all.  This is what serves Styx,
#	           runs in a pipeline, or sits in a login session.
#
# Why they must be separate rather than one binary used both ways:
# macOS App Nap SUSPENDS a Cocoa app that has no window on screen.  A
# headless emu-cocoa serving Styx froze entirely -- connections
# completing in the kernel and queueing unaccepted, handshakes
# unanswered for minutes, CPU time frozen, SIGTERM ignored, then
# recovery with no explanation.  eleven runs of tools/jtag/wedgewatch.sh
# failed that way.  A process with no NSApplication cannot be napped,
# which is a stronger guarantee than asking politely not to be.
#
